\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces High-level system architecture showing the eight pipeline stages from query input to response output.}}{17}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.2}{\ignorespaces Hybrid retrieval component architecture showing BM25 and dense retrieval paths, RRF fusion, source diversity filtering, and dynamic-$k$ selection.}}{19}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.3}{\ignorespaces XAI module architecture showing the five confidence signals and their combination via Platt scaling into a preliminarily calibrated score.}}{20}{}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Eight-stage RAG pipeline. Each evaluation query enters at Stage 1 (query enhancement) and exits at Stage 8 carrying a confidence-scored, source-attributed response. The dashed red path is the re-retrieval loop triggered when the grounding gate rejects the initial context.}}{23}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces System interaction sequence from API request receipt through retrieval, generation, confidence scoring, and response serialisation.}}{26}{}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces Data ingestion pipeline from raw source datasets through text cleaning, sentence-boundary chunking, and embedding to the ChromaDB vector store and BM25 pickle cache.}}{29}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces Metric comparison across the three generation backends (TinyLlama base, QLoRA fine-tuned TinyLlama, and BioMistral-7B). QLoRA achieves the highest keyword coverage; BioMistral leads on ROUGE-L and BERTScore.}}{31}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.3}{\ignorespaces Deployment architecture: GitHub Actions CI pipeline triggers on push to main (lint and test); Docker Compose brings up the FastAPI backend and Streamlit frontend with ChromaDB and the BM25 index persisted on a shared volume.}}{32}{}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.1}{\ignorespaces Metric comparison across generation backends. While \ac {qlora} fine-tuning delivered the most significant boost to keyword coverage, BioMistral consistently outperformed the other models in \ac {rouge}-L and \ac {bert_score} metrics.}}{35}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.2}{\ignorespaces Ablation impact on keyword coverage. We can see how coverage drops as each signal is pulled out. Source agreement clearly has the most influence on the final score.}}{36}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.3}{\ignorespaces Confidence calibration for the raw system. In a perfect setup, the points would follow the diagonal line. Instead, our system is consistently cautious, underestimating its own accuracy across every bin.}}{39}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.4}{\ignorespaces Latency across pipeline stages. Retrieval and generation take up most of the 115-second total, taking 42.6s and 69.9s respectively. Everything else finishes in under 3 seconds.}}{39}{}%
